{number: 172}
{title: Near to the Heart of God}
{key: Db}

{start_of_verse: 1}
There is a [Db] place of quiet [Gb] rest,
[Db] Near to the heart of [Ab7] God;
A place where [Db] sin cannot mo-[Gb] lest,
[Db] Near to the [Ab7] heart of [Db] God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
O [Gb] Jesus, blest Re-[Db] deemer,
Sent [Ab7] from the heart of [Db] God,
Hold [Db] us who wait be-[Gb] fore Thee
[Db] Near to the [Ab7] heart of [Db] God.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
There is a [Db] place of comfort [Gb] sweet,
[Db] Near to the heart of [Ab7] God;
A place where [Db] we our Savior [Gb] meet,
[Db] Near to the [Ab7] heart of [Db] God.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
There is a [Db] place of full re-[Gb] lease,
[Db] Near to the heart of [Ab7] God;
A place where [Db] all is joy and [Gb] peace,
[Db] Near to the [Ab7] heart of [Db] God.
{end_of_verse}
